  --required-conversation-resolution: oneof<nothing, bool> # Requires all conversations on code to be resolved before a pull request can be merged into a branch that matches this rule. Set to `false` to disable. Default: `false`.
  --required-linear-history: oneof<nothing, bool> # Enforces a linear commit Git history, which prevents anyone from pushing merge commits to a branch. Set to `true` to enforce a linear commit history. Set to `false` to disable a linear commit Git history. Your repository must allow squash merging or rebase merging before you can enable a linear commit history. Default: `false`. For more information, see "[Requiring a linear commit history](https://docs.github.com/enterprise-cloud@latest//github/administering-a-repository/requiring-a-linear-commit-history)" in the GitHub Help documentation.
